course: dictionary
lesson: 11804
title: Formal words and what they show
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to formal writing, such as classic stories and exam texts. Betoken is one of them. It means to be a sign of something, or to show that something is true or is going to happen. «Dark clouds betoken a storm» means the dark clouds are a sign that a storm is coming.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A smile betokens friendship» tells you a smile is a sign of friendship. Check your meaning by swapping in a simple phrase: «A smile is a sign of friendship» makes the same sense, so you have understood betoken.
explain: Betoken is a verb, so it changes like other verbs: betokens, betokened, betokening. «The wet footprints betokened that someone had been there.» Betokened is the past tense: the footprints were a sign that a person had passed by.
explain: In everyday talk, people say «be a sign of» or «show» instead. Writers use betoken to sound formal and old-fashioned, so when you meet it, read it as a fancy way of saying shows.
fact: Betoken means to be a sign of something.
fact: Betoken is a formal word, found in classic stories and exam texts.
fact: «Dark clouds betoken a storm» means dark clouds are a sign that a storm is coming.
fact: «A smile betokens friendship» means a smile shows that someone is friendly.
fact: Everyday words that mean the same as betoken are «be a sign of» and «show».
exercise: «Dark clouds betoken a storm.» What does betoken mean here? | To wash something away | To fall quickly | To hide something | *To be a sign of something
exercise: «A smile betokens friendship.» Which everyday phrase could replace betokens? | measures | *is a sign of | drops | forgets
exercise: «The wet footprints betokened a visitor.» Which word shows the past tense of betoken? | betokens | betokening | *betokened | betoken
test: «The grey sky betokens rain.» What does betokens mean? | *Is a sign that rain is coming | Is a sign that the sun will shine | Is far away from rain | Is a type of cloud
test: Which sentence means the same as «Her tears betoken sadness»? | Her tears hide her sadness | Her tears are a kind of rain | *Her tears are a sign of sadness | Her tears wash away sadness
exam: Which sentence uses betoken correctly? | Thick smoke betoken a fire nearby is my favourite | I betoken my homework yesterday | Betokens the smoke a fire nearby | *Thick smoke betokens a fire nearby
